  "summary": "CT list for Mon 10/26 at St. Brigid Imaging. Four studies are booked; appointments appt-00006, appt-00001 and appt-00008 are cancelled, so they were left off.\n\n- pt-0047 Britt Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001): No allergies. He has diabetes and his last creatinine (9/24) was more than 30 days old, so I ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0009). An outside creatinine from 10/22 then arrived: 1.52 (eGFR 64), up from 0.94. This doesn't meet the policy's definition of acute kidney injury (AKI), so no IV fluids are needed. I kept the pre-scan creatinine order. He has the instructions and an update; follow-up task to you about the rise (task-t0024).\n- pt-0015 Daniel Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0002): The 2019 radiology report rates his iohexol reaction as moderate. The allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\", but under the policy that doesn't change the grade. Premedication ordered: prednisone 50 mg at Sun 20:00, Mon 02:00 and 08:00, plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at Mon 08:00 (mr-t0007/t0008). He needs a driver. The lab later corrected his 10/14 creatinine from 0.98 (another patient's sample) to 2.8, eGFR 24. So I added 500 mL 0.9% saline IV starting at 08:00 (mr-t0018) and sent a corrected message in Spanish and English: arrive by 08:00. Task to you to work up the new eGFR (task-t0023).\n- pt-0049 Anisha Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0003): She had AKI on 10/4 that hasn't been shown back to baseline. Ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0010) and 500 mL 0.9% saline IV starting at 12:00 (mr-t0005). Metformin (mr-00392) is on hold: no doses on 10/26 or for 48 hours after, and it restarts only once a kidney recheck is normal (task-t0015). A 2022 outside report then arrived showing a moderate reaction to iopamidol. Added premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00, plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0016/t0017). She needs a driver; updated instructions sent. Iopamidol isn't in the catalog, so it couldn't be added to her allergy list.\n- pt-0046 Lauren Beahan, 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast (sr-t0004): Ordered as booked, and she was told no prep is needed. A 2024 outside report showed a mild reaction to iohexol; I added it to her allergy list (alg-t0019). That doesn't change this non-contrast scan.\n\nI wrote a note under RBC-RAD-07 for each patient and closed the four new inbox items. There were no other new arrivals.",
